{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CffBp3DCZ6BJHKGTjiGAD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The candidate passed the self-check (`OK`), but it is unlikely to beat the current best model. Its smoke-fit ELPD-LOO was about −2634, against −2383 for the incumbent `balance_aware_heads_alternation_ideal`.\n\n**Model: `max_lopsided_window_surprise`.** It follows the brief's \"single most salient local feature\" idea. Each sequence is judged by its one most lopsided stretch:\n- It looks at every contiguous stretch of two or more flips.\n- For each stretch, it measures how unlikely that stretch's heads/tails split is for a fair coin of that length, in bits.\n- The **maximum** over all stretches decides how non-random the sequence looks. The rest of the sequence does not count.\n- A person picks the sequence whose worst stretch is less surprising. How strongly that difference drives the choice varies by person (a group-level average with individual deviations, sized for 400 participant slots so the design can predict new participants).\n\nThis targets the critique point that held up after correcting for multiple tests: at equal switch counts, people pick the sequence with the shorter longest run. A stretch like HHTHHH, nearly all one face but broken up, counts too, which a plain longest-run measure misses.\n\n**How it differs from what's been tried.** It is distinct from the pruned `most_salient_regular_stretch` and from the streak-excess penalties. It measures lopsided splits in the sense of fair-coin probability, and it has no switching-rate ideal.\n\n**Main weakness.** The model scores perfect alternation (HTHTHTHT) as maximally random, because no stretch in it is lopsided. That is part of what it tests, but it is also the likely reason it fits worse.\n\n**Check details.**\n- Smoke fit: 100 draws, 1 chain.\n- The check warned that LOO is unreliable (6.9% of trials have a high Pareto-k) and that R-hat can't be computed from a single chain. Both may be artefacts of the short fit; the full admission fit will settle convergence.\n- Novelty against the other models was not checked.\n\nThe three files are in `experiment2/model_loop/iter_1/candidate_0/`: `hypothesis.md`, `model_name.txt` and `candidate.py`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2335,"cache_read_input_tokens":62344,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2335,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e9171a21-21ac-46fd-b638-3f297c231d7f","uuid":"92de5d00-4fe4-403f-bcec-60a7b01d767f","timestamp":"2026-10-03T10:59:56.156Z","request_id":"req_011CffBp2ZzwjmDZmGx1yJdH"}
